Morphology: after thresholding, there may be tiny unwanted dots, holes, broken boundaries and small gaps. so we need the clean mask. 
Process image based on the shape and structure of regions
Morphology is used to clean, repair, connect, or separate shapes in a binary image.
It deals with the shape of the object 
4 main operations:
a. Erosion: shrink object
b. dilation: expand object
c. Opening: E--D means to remove noise
d. Closing: D--E means fill gaps and holes

Contour: Object Boundaries
Shape Analaysis: Shape analyse krna

Contour: Means Boundary of the Object:
Connected Component Analysis: Which pixel belong to the same object/region. So we calculate: Perimeter/Area/ Bounding Reactangle: We can put a rectangle around the object/ Centroid: appr center of the object[Useful for tracking]
Aspect Ratio: Width/Height: Use when search for rectabgular regions such as license plate candidates.
Extent: tells us how much of the bounding box is occupied by the actaul object. extent=contour area/bounding reactangle area
Solidity: Solidity compares the object's area with its convex hull area. solidity=contour area/convex hull area
It tells us how solid/compact an object is compared with the smallest convex shape that can completely cover it.
example: object area = 800 and convex hull area = 1000 then solidity = 0.8 so 80% of the area enclosed by its convex hull.
why need? as different objects can have different shapes. so these numbers give you info about their shape. it is one shape feature so do not use this alone to identify object
Roundness/Circularity: 4pieA/p*p. Perfect value close to 1. Lower than 1 more irregular.
Image Moments: describe how pixels are distributed in a region.Higher-order moments can also describe the distribution of the shape.
Hu Moments:relatively invariant to transformation such as translation/scaling/rotation.
Hu Moments provide a compact numerical signature of a shape that can be useful for shape comparison

contour hierarchy: outer contour and inner contour. if an object contain another boundary inside it. Get two variable: contours- contains the actual contour points and hierarchy contains the relationship between those contours.It has 4 hierarchy values: Next, Previous, First_child, Parent.
example: Contour 0--Outer Boundary of A
contour 1-- Hole inside A
contour 2-- Outer Boundary of B
RETR_EXTERNAL: retrieves only outermost contours
RETR_TREE: retrieves the complete hiearchy

Connected Components:foreground pixels are connected and belong to the same region. It assigns a unique label to each connected region. Area/ Centroid/ Bounding Box/ Width and Height and Labels

